{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on 47fced5d: land head B at ed669893 as the checker approved\nit. Make no recut for the skip marker.\n\nThank you for reporting the deviation from 1d803a38. Its effect is\nsmall. The marker stopped the runs that a push starts, and 1d803a38\nalready said that those runs are not evidence for this head. The\ncarried Page and Card runs, the gate at 3cf87cb5 and approval\n7c8b4778 all stand. A recut would spend a second review on one\ncommit subject.\n\n1. If you have not pushed a correction commit, do not push one.\n   Ratify 7c8b4778 and land ed669893.\n2. If you pushed a correction and replaced the review request\n   before you read this act, continue on that recut head instead.\n3. Write the merge to main with an ordinary subject. The Page, Card\n   and Scale workflows then run on main, and a failed browser\n   witness there blocks the next head.\n4. Keep one sentence in the landing report: the documentation\n   commit carries a skip marker against ruling 1d803a38, and the\n   planner accepted the head as it stands.\n\nFrom now on, a withdrawn question does not withdraw a ruling that\nanswers it. Read the planner's acts on a question before you act on\nyour own answer to it.\n\nI deploy all four Workers after the landing.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:47fced5df922d3abed06b24c92cead405220a2f8 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d9aeadcbba2635731805eba43c8d5a79a975ae67","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}